Subject: [PATCH] AROS host: LightCraft in an Intuition window through
 egui-aros

apps/lightcraft-aros runs the egui interface with egui-aros: winit and egui-winit for the window and input, the CPU renderer or OpenGL chosen at run time (--gui-renderer, ToolType GUI_RENDERER, the GUI_RENDERER variable; AUTO by default), ASL requesters for files and folders. It follows the desktop app's start-up: settings (upstream's prefs.rs, used as it is), the library chosen by --library, LIGHTCRAFT_LIBRARY, Settings or the default location, the library-problem window, files and drawers from the Shell or Workbench resolved by DOS and imported. Settings, the log and the default library live in LightCraftData beside the program (LIGHTCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR), the folder upstream's portable mode and the 0.13.0 port use. The program runs in the -nix path mode; requesters' DOS names are converted at the edge. Not on AROS: the control server, the lens database download, links and other programs. --screenshot and --test-steps (control requests at given frames) are test aids.
